# Repo layout and runtime

## What lives where

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `envs/<task>.py` | Task class: spawn, expert `play_once`, `check_success` |
| `assets/dyna_assets/` | Custom RoboDyna object meshes + office fixtures (shelf, file holder) |
| `assets/dyna_textures/` | Custom images / textures (logos, stamps, soccer ball, README gifs) |
| `assets/objects/` | Stock RoboTwin object library (HF download, gitignored) |
| `assets/background_texture/` | Stock wall/table texture library (HF download, gitignored) |
| `envs/utils/` | Task runtime helpers plus asset/task-creation CLI scripts |
| `task_config/*.yml` | Configs; stock tree mostly gitignored — use `demo_*.yml` / `_*.yml` |
| `description/task_instruction/<task>.json` | Language instructions |
| `interactive/` | Shared helpers + GUI launchers (`base_task_gui.py`, `household_task_gui.py`) |
| `interactive/base/` | Base suite interactive runners (`interactive_<task>.py`) |
| `interactive/household/` | Household interactive runners + `_interactive_common.py` |
| `interactive/tests/` | One-off probes, smoke tests, and helper record scripts |
| `tests/` | Suite success sweeps, gallery demo publish, and regression tests |
| `script/bench_script/record_demo.py` | Shared demo recorder |
| `docs/final_task_demos/` | Curated gallery clips (side-by-side GIFs/MP4s, snapshots) |
| `tmp/` / `tmp/tmp_<task>/` | Local scratch for demos, sweeps, probes (gitignored except keep) |
| `task_gallery` (sibling repo under `Desktop/RoboReal/`) | Published web gallery; sync demos there when updating README cards |

Do not dump probe scripts, one-off mp4s, or sweep junk into `docs/final_task_demos/` or repo root — use `tmp/`.

## Skills to follow

- New / extended tasks or objects → `.claude/skills/SAPIEN-task-creator`
- Demo video after task work → `.claude/skills/record-video-demo`
- Interactive viewers → keep 2s wall-clock hold after terminal success/failure (see `interactive-post-success-hold.mdc`)

## Physics / grasp sanity (always)

From project practice (`basic_prompt.md`):

- Spawned objects must not collide or overlap at init.
- Prefer real physics: no silent teleport/attach of grasped objects; fingers close **around** the object, not through it.
- Round objects roll; non-round objects slip on tilt when that is the intended contact model.
- Objects should not appear/disappear without an explicit task mechanic.

## Naming

CLI / env class name must match `envs/<task>.py`. Alias: `place_block_task` → `place_block_belt`.
